+ * it lives at the call site as the `fallback` argument of `t()`, so a key
+ * missing from this file renders English by construction.
+ *
+ * Rules followed here — see GLOSSARY_RU.md:
+ *   - only user-facing strings; code, identifiers, CLI commands, paths, URLs,
+ *     model/provider/brand names and log lines stay in English;
+ *   - `{placeholders}` are copied verbatim, including their names;
+ *   - plural keys are `key.one` / `key.few` / `key.many` / `key.other`,
+ *     selected through `Intl.PluralRules('ru')`;
+ *   - «ё» is written out in full and quotation uses «…», per Russian
+ *     typography.
+ *
+ * `i18n/__tests__/locale-catalog.test.ts` enforces the mechanical half of
+ * this: no duplicate keys, well-formed keys, at least one Cyrillic letter per
